==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gross Koi Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Kiss and Koi''' when obtained from [[Koi Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Koi Cat is similar to [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], but with far less damage, less health, and single target. These issues render him outright useless outside of [[Empire of Cats]] besides the fact that he is part of some surprisingly good Cat Combos, as explained below.

Koi Cat's role is a Combo slave, meaning you only bring him into battle for the Combos. [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] and [[Team of Two (Combo)|Team of Two]] are both quite strong. The former is very useful and can be combined with [[Lion King (Combo)|Lion King]] and [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]], allowing you to have three strong Cat Combos. This is his only use, but it is quite helpful, empowering [[:Category:Cats with Strong ability|Cats with Strong against abilities]] by a large margin against their targeted traits.

==='''True Form'''===
Kiss and Koi receive Area Attack, but also a much higher speed, making them rush into enemy range and be torn to pieces. This significantly impairs stackability, stripping Kiss and Koi of even basic midranger utility and any sort of remedy to their awful dps.

The only time Kiss and Koi could be useful is when paired with Cat Combos to rush down [[Hannya]], but not using them in battle would be a better idea. The speed increase is only a drawback, and that, plus the lack of new Combos makes Kiss and Koi even worse than their Evolved form.

