==Trivia==
*Koi Cat looks like a decorative koi banner (鯉のぼり, koinobori). This type of decoration is often seen in Japan around Golden Week, in honor of [[Love is Sickness (Monthly Event)|Children's Day]].
**This may also be the reason for the long legs of the Evolved and [[True Form]]s, as the koinobori banners are hung up high on a pole, which slightly resembles the legs.
*Koi means both "love" and "carp" in Japanese, therefore the design of the cat include a koi banner (which is designed to be carp-like), the unit is in [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] and Kiss and Koi's description mentions love.
*Koi Cat's Japanese name, Maji de Koishiteru, is a reference to the song "[https://youtu.be/pG0bviOCSH0 Maji De Koi Suru 5byoumae]" by [[wikipedia:Ryōko Hirosue|Ryōko Hirosue]].

